Implemented behavior:
- BodySource-backed passthrough reuses the captured source instead of allocating a second request body.
- SQLite usage writes maintain exact hourly rollups; dashboard responses use 5-second fresh / 60-second stale-while-revalidate snapshots.
- Standard transports, in-process TLS clients, and cookie jars are bounded by memory tier and expose aggregate hit/miss/eviction metrics.
- Scheduler hot load counters are split across 64 shards; candidate indexes publish without whole-map copies; bounded egress TTFT/success EWMA affects outlet selection; deadline races preserve the real pinned-account wait reason.
- The selected locale is a lazy chunk, Pool UI imports are tree-shakeable, heavy automatic prefetch is disabled, and production assets are Brotli-precompressed with gzip fallback.
- SSE sends the first event immediately, then batches complete events at 4 KiB or 3 ms, retaining an 8 KiB tail bound and a supervised timer callback.

